  "body": "**What happens:** on current main, `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test continuous_4axis_part` fails:\n\n```\npanicked at crates/app/tests/continuous_4axis_part.rs:162:9:\nexamples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj is stale; regenerate with WRITE_GOLDEN=1: /version: 71 != 70\n```\n\n**Cause:** merge 4b1629b3b (PR #2134, DXF sketch import, 2026-11-18 22:14 UTC) raised `PROJECT_VERSION` from 67 to 71 (`crates/app/src/project/file.rs:143`). The test saves the example project and compares it with the committed `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj`, which still says `\"version\": 70`. The other examples are not compared by version.\n\n**Found by:** mkinney's merge train (batch tier on main 51a00c4ae + #2122; the only failure). The hourly main-health check (clippy + xtask tests) does not run this suite, so it stayed green.\n\n**Fix:** regenerate with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test continuous_4axis_part`, then check that the regenerated `.nc` program golden is byte-identical (only the project file's version and new default fields should change). If the posted program changes, stop and report: that would be a behaviour change from #2134.\n\nDone means: `continuous_4axis_part` passes on main, and the committed `.nc` golden is unchanged (or each changed line is explained).\n",
